@@ -64,6 +64,20 @@ These formats can be lowercase (`minutes`), uppercase (`MINUTES`), or capitalize
 
 If no unit is passed (`2`), the unit will default to `Milliseconds`.  Fractional input values like `0.5m`, `-0.5m`, `.5m`, and `-.5m` are supported.
 
+### Compound Durations
+
+Use `parseCompound` to sum several `<number><unit>` parts. Parts can be separated by whitespace, a comma, or both.
+
+```ts
+import { parseCompound } from 'ms'
+
+parseCompound('1h 30m')          // 5400000
+parseCompound('1h, 30m')         // 5400000
+parseCompound('2 days 4 hours')  // 187200000
+```
+
+Every part needs a unit. It throws a `TypeError` for invalid input and never returns `NaN`.
+
 ## Installation
 
 You can install this package using a package manager like [npm](https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v11/commands/npm-install), [yarn](https://yarnpkg.com/cli/add), [pnpm](https://pnpm.io/cli/add), [deno](https://docs.deno.com/runtime/reference/cli/add), or [bun](https://bun.com/docs/cli/add).
